tic primary, while Anthony DiLorenzo took the Republican nomination. Both candidates raised roughly $2.4 million, but Shaheen holds more cash on hand and benefits from about $2.2 million in outside support backing her campaign.\n\nNo general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets. Raters mostly call the race Likely D, with a few at Lean D or stronger. Prediction markets put Shaheen's chances around 91 percent. The district's swing history keeps some uncertainty, but the evidence points to a clear Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.937, "margin": 10.01}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9238, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9245, "margin": 9.5}]}